From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rita Zhang <rita.zhang@coreweave.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Backport vllm#49016: bump MSA GIT_TAG for CUTLASS DSL 4.6.0

vLLM 0.26.0 pins nvidia-cutlass-dsl==4.6.0 (via requirements/cuda.txt),
which removed the deprecated `cutlass.cute.core.ThrMma` alias. The MSA
commit pinned in fmha_sm100.cmake (2e63ec37...) still references that
symbol via `vllm/third_party/fmha_sm100/cute/src/common/utils.py:156`,
so serving MiniMax-M3 (and other models routing through the SM100
sparse FMHA backend) crashes at engine init with:

    AttributeError: module 'cutlass.cute.core' has no attribute 'ThrMma'

MSA PR vllm-project/MSA#8 (merge sha 890aaa1a...) rewrites the affected
sites to use `cute.ThrMma` and applies other CUTLASS DSL 4.6 compat
fixes. vLLM PR vllm-project/vllm#49016 (merged to main 2026-07-21)
bumped the pinned GIT_TAG accordingly, but was not backported to the
releases/v0.26.0 branch this image tracks — hence this local patch.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49016
Bug report:   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/49005

Signed-off-by: Rita Zhang <rita.zhang@coreweave.com>
---
 cmake/external_projects/fmha_sm100.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/external_projects/fmha_sm100.cmake b/cmake/external_projects/fmha_sm100.cmake
--- a/cmake/external_projects/fmha_sm100.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external_projects/fmha_sm100.cmake
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ else()
   FetchContent_Declare(
     fmha_sm100
     GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/vllm-project/MSA.git
-    GIT_TAG 2e63ec37a0fc29bc20f39cd1a52e0f5affc33a73
+    GIT_TAG 890aaa1a37a598ad17ccff0827fea21540d381fa
     GIT_PROGRESS TRUE
     CONFIGURE_COMMAND ""
     BUILD_COMMAND ""
